# The Session data

## Independent curated edition

This fork is maintained by [andyxuhang](https://github.com/andyxuhang) and contains reviewed ABC notation corrections. The first round corrects six settings across five tunes. See [the review and evidence](REVIEW.md), [the exact correction manifest](corrections/round-001.json), and [the validation results](corrections/round-001-validation.json).

The source baseline is [adactio/TheSession-data at 9106aa8](https://github.com/adactio/TheSession-data/tree/9106aa8e29b72c3affd954f48b259ea02a1fb418). This is an independent edition. Original contributors are credited in the data. The database continues under ODbL 1.0, with the full upstream content terms preserved in [LICENSE.md](LICENSE.md).

CSV, JSON and SQLite exports include the same corrections. The [reproduction tool](tools/apply_corrections.py) applies only the exact reviewed changes and validates the representations. Each future upstream update should be checked against the recorded source hashes before reapplying a correction.

## Upstream project information

CSV and JSON files of data from [The Session](https://thesession.org/):

* [tunes](https://thesession.org/tunes/),
* [sessions](https://thesession.org/sessions/),
* [events](https://thesession.org/events/),
* [recordings](https://thesession.org/recordings/),
* [sets of tunes](https://thesession.org/tunes/sets),
* aliases of tune names,
* popularity of tunes.

I'll try to update the files once a week.

If anyone wants to convert the data to other formats, feel free to fork the project and send me a pull request.

If this data is useful to you, please [donate money to the upkeep of The Session](https://thesession.org/donate).
